;; spec:   stdlib §1.2 P3 (in place when unique), §2.5, §4.4 row pop, tranche 2 plan Y5 and P1
;; expect: accept
;; result: 600
;; audit:  clean
;; allocs: <= 2000
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: pop
;; open:   P1
;; 600 pops from a Vec of 640. Today each pop rebuilds the rest, so the run allocates one rebuild a pop, about 2 objects for
;; every 32 elements left and a few more: 20773 in all (measured, the interpreter's count), and the bound of 2000 fails: the case is OPEN.
;; When task P1 lands the prelude's vec-pop (the tail first, then the last leaf of the trie: a new tail array and a new header
;; per pop, about 6 on the pop that takes the last leaf out of the trie), the one line of Y5's Vec instance that calls the
;; rebuild is swapped for it, a run is 54 objects for the vector and about 2.1 a pop, near 1300, the bound holds, the case
;; passes, and the commit that swaps the line removes the open label (and sets the bound to the measured count). The bound is
;; worked out by hand for that day, not run.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq fib.coll))

(defun main () -> i64
  (loop ((v (vec (range 640))) (n 0))
    (if (< n 600) (recur (pop v) (+ n 1)) (- 640 (count v)))))
